      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "AI Assisted Operations",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "AI Assisted Operations",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "MlcyUL9dDx8CBgjjU9n2o",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 120.70668134653675,
      "y": 1180.7189934297735,
      "width": 998.3390502929688,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#4dabf7",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aB",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 59303008,
      "version": 925,
      "versionNonce": 1980053920,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1776518387134,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Space management involves typical the typical flows of managing the organizations and projects\nin which the application is contained. In capybara cloud, since these functionalities are tightly related,\nthey are generalized into the \"Space\" module.    \n\nThis concept of \"space\" aims to first group related resources togherher, and second, \nto limit whom have access to what resources. ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Space management involves typical the typical flows of managing the organizations and projects\nin which the application is contained. In capybara cloud, since these functionalities are tightly related,\nthey are generalized into the \"Space\" module.    \n\nThis concept of \"space\" aims to first group related resources togherher, and second, \nto limit whom have access to what resources. ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "xPSQslZ9mWSwQPFUez_Bi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 99.51051276804043,
      "y": 1639.714144908412,
      "width": 946.8590087890625,
      "height": 650,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#4dabf7",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aBV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 832357472,
      "version": 3819,
      "versionNonce": 600622201,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1776725958761,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The deployment and operation of applications (and to do them easiliy and reliably) \nis the core functionality of Capybara Cloud (or any PaaS).\n\nIn order to deploy and run applications, we need:\n- Information about the applications (Runtime environment, env vars, resource requirements, etc).\n- How and where are these applications going to be deployed (Hosts).\n- Expose limited access to these hosts (e.g expose only specific ports on the hosts).\n\nTwo separate modules\n\nTherefore, the Deployment module exposes the following APIs:\n- Create deployment.\n- Retrieve the status & Result of the deployment.\n- Stop/Delete deployment.\n\nInternally, in order to implement these APIs, the deployment module has to implement\nthe following mechanisms:\n\n- It needs to find where this application could be deployed (finding a host).\n- It registers a request to this host to run the application, passing the app's metadata.\n- It should then work together with this host to monitor the state of application.\n- If the application was terminated, and the host, for some reasons could not resume \nthe operation of the app, or worse, does not respond at all, this module should\nimplement some kind of algorithm to move the operation to another host. \n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The deployment and operation of applications (and to do them easiliy and reliably) \nis the core functionality of Capybara Cloud (or any PaaS).\n\nIn order to deploy and run applications, we need:\n- Information about the applications (Runtime environment, env vars, resource requirements, etc).\n- How and where are these applications going to be deployed (Hosts).\n- Expose limited access to these hosts (e.g expose only specific ports on the hosts).\n\nTwo separate modules\n\nTherefore, the Deployment module exposes the following APIs:\n- Create deployment.\n- Retrieve the status & Result of the deployment.\n- Stop/Delete deployment.\n\nInternally, in order to implement these APIs, the deployment module has to implement\nthe following mechanisms:\n\n- It needs to find where this application could be deployed (finding a host).\n- It registers a request to this host to run the application, passing the app's metadata.\n- It should then work together with this host to monitor the state of application.\n- If the application was terminated, and the host, for some reasons could not resume \nthe operation of the app, or worse, does not respond at all, this module should\nimplement some kind of algorithm to move the operation to another host. \n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "YOqI-lIwNH0Rek3vbIpwL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 93.76862738314054,
      "y": 2380.482121063916,
      "width": 1108.5189208984375,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#4dabf7",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aBZ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1867031648,
      "version": 4609,
      "versionNonce": 1028240480,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1776520662596,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Hosts are the physical/virtual machines on top of which applications are deployed. There are multiple ways\nof provisioning machines to serve as the application infrastructure, the easiest being to rely on popular cloud\ninfrastructure providers such as AWS, GCP, and Allibaba Cloud. In Capybara Cloud, we offer another way to\nto provide infrastructure, by bringing OUR OWN server.\n\nIn order to join provisioning (i.e being recognized as host), these machines \"tell\" the provisioning service\nthat they have some free resources and are ready to run applications. The provisioning service would later then, \ntell the host to pull application metadata and start the application associated with a deployment.\n\n ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Hosts are the physical/virtual machines on top of which applications are deployed. There are multiple ways\nof provisioning machines to serve as the application infrastructure, the easiest being to rely on popular cloud\ninfrastructure providers such as AWS, GCP, and Allibaba Cloud. In Capybara Cloud, we offer another way to\nto provide infrastructure, by bringing OUR OWN server.\n\nIn order to join provisioning (i.e being recognized as host), these machines \"tell\" the provisioning service\nthat they have some free resources and are ready to run applications. The provisioning service would later then, \ntell the host to pull application metadata and start the application associated with a deployment.\n\n ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "W_W9PuHQpzPl5r5Gcq3ip",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 116.09340009653675,
      "y": 1370.8203423067266,
      "width": 396.4996643066406,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#4dabf7",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aC",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 113497504,
      "version": 1110,
      "versionNonce": 1140543904,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1776518387134,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "This module exposes the following APIs:\n- CRUD organizations.\n- CRUD projects.\n- CRUD applications.    ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "This module exposes the following APIs:\n- CRUD organizations.\n- CRUD projects.\n- CRUD applications.    ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ZfJZJ3aYpiAV5JicwtjwS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 84.26439535779915,
      "y": 2758.677918637993,
      "width": 1003.0791015625,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#4dabf7",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aD",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1754168736,
      "version": 297,
      "versionNonce": 381097376,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1776520963482,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "To make the entire process of managing space, deploying apps into them easy, Capybara Cloud exposes\n\"tools\" for AI Agents to consume and interact with.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "To make the entire process of managing space, deploying apps into them easy, Capybara Cloud exposes\n\"tools\" for AI Agents to consume and interact with.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
